### ==========================================================
### SYNC — tirón incremental y snapshot inicial (mirror offline)
### Un solo endpoint: sin `since` ni `cursor` = snapshot completo.
### Trae ARCHIVADOS y BORRADOS (archivedAt / deletedAt): es la única
### forma de que el cliente se entere de que algo desapareció.
### Orden (updatedAt, _id); `limit` cuenta filas de TODAS las entidades.
### El `nextCursor` de un tirón terminado va 60 s por detrás de
### `serverTime` a propósito: `updatedAt` lo estampa la app, no la BD.
### ==========================================================
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@email = tester@test.com
@password = SecureP@ss123

# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

###

@token = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Snapshot completo (primer arranque del cliente)
# @name snapshot
GET {{baseUrl}}/sync/changes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

@nextCursor = {{snapshot.response.body.pagination.nextCursor}}

### Tirón incremental: el nextCursor del anterior, tal cual
GET {{baseUrl}}/sync/changes?cursor={{nextCursor}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Página pequeña para ver el paginado (hasMore = true)
# @name firstPage
GET {{baseUrl}}/sync/changes?limit=2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

@pageCursor = {{firstPage.response.body.pagination.nextCursor}}

### Segunda página — no repite ni se salta filas en el borde
GET {{baseUrl}}/sync/changes?limit=2&cursor={{pageCursor}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Por fecha en vez de cursor: `since` es EXCLUSIVO
GET {{baseUrl}}/sync/changes?since=2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Acepta offset ISO (mismo instante que el de arriba en Bogotá)
GET {{baseUrl}}/sync/changes?since=2025-12-31T19:00:00-05:00
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Si llegan los dos, gana `cursor` (es la posición más precisa)
GET {{baseUrl}}/sync/changes?since=1999-01-01T00:00:00.000Z&cursor={{nextCursor}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Archivar una cuenta y volver a tirar: aparece con archivedAt
### (crea la cuenta, archívala, y pide los cambios desde antes)
# @name syncAcc
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Sync demo {{$randomInt 100 999}}", "type": "CASH", "balance": 10 }

###

@syncAccId = {{syncAcc.response.body.id}}

### Archivarla
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{syncAccId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Ahora aparece en el feed con archivedAt != null
GET {{baseUrl}}/sync/changes?since=2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---------- Casos de error ----------

### Cursor ilegible (400, code INVALID_CURSOR) — NO devuelve la página 1
GET {{baseUrl}}/sync/changes?cursor=no-es-un-cursor
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### limit por encima del techo (400, code VALIDATION, field "limit")
GET {{baseUrl}}/sync/changes?limit=5000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### limit 0 (400, code VALIDATION)
GET {{baseUrl}}/sync/changes?limit=0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### since sin hora (400, code VALIDATION)
GET {{baseUrl}}/sync/changes?since=2026-01-01
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Sin token (401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/sync/changes

### ==========================================================
### POST /sync — el outbox offline como UN lote (O-B4)
### Cada operación se contesta por separado: applied | duplicate |
### conflict | rejected | blocked (merged queda reservado). El 200 solo
### dice que el sobre era válido; el resultado va en results[i].status.
### payload.body es el body de la ruta equivalente; baseUpdatedAt es su
### If-Match; payload.query.reference es el reference de budgets.
### Límites: 1–200 operaciones, 1 MB, opVersion 1.
### ==========================================================

### Lote: crear una cuenta y un gasto que depende de ella (applied, applied)
# @name syncBatch
POST {{baseUrl}}/sync
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "operations": [
    {
      "opId": "{{$guid}}",
      "seq": 1,
      "occurredAt": "2026-09-05T10:00:00.000Z",
      "entity": "account",
      "action": "create",
      "id": "0195a000-0000-7000-8000-00000000{{$randomInt 1000 9999}}",
      "payload": { "body": { "name": "Batch {{$randomInt 100 999}}", "type": "CASH", "balance": 100 } },
      "dependsOn": [],
      "opVersion": 1
    }
  ]
}

###

@batchAccId = {{syncBatch.response.body.results[0].id}}
@batchAccVersion = {{syncBatch.response.body.results[0].result.updatedAt}}

### El mismo opId otra vez → duplicate (no se aplica nada). Copia el opId de
### la respuesta anterior en lugar de {{$guid}} para verlo.
# POST {{baseUrl}}/sync
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# { "operations": [ { "opId": "<opId de arriba>", "seq": 1, "occurredAt": "2026-09-05T10:00:00.000Z",
#     "entity": "account", "action": "create", "id": "{{batchAccId}}",
#     "payload": { "body": { "name": "Da igual", "type": "CASH", "balance": 1 } }, "opVersion": 1 } ] }

### Gasto sobre la cuenta del lote anterior, con dependsOn (applied)
POST {{baseUrl}}/sync
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "operations": [
    {
      "opId": "{{$guid}}",
      "seq": 2,
      "occurredAt": "2026-09-05T10:01:00.000Z",
      "entity": "transaction",
      "action": "create",
      "id": "{{$guid}}",
      "payload": { "body": { "type": "EXPENSE", "amount": 12.5, "date": "2026-09-01T12:00:00.000Z", "fromAccountId": "{{batchAccId}}" } },
      "dependsOn": ["{{batchAccId}}"],
      "opVersion": 1
    }
  ]
}

### Renombrar en otro dispositivo (mueve updatedAt)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{batchAccId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Renombrada en otro sitio {{$randomInt 100 999}}" }

### Lote con 409 dentro: update con baseUpdatedAt viejo → conflict STALE_UPDATE
### con `current`; el archive de la misma fila sale blocked (blockedBy = opId
### del update); la categoría independiente sale applied.
POST {{baseUrl}}/sync
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "operations": [
    {
      "opId": "0195a000-0000-7000-8000-0000000000a1",
      "seq": 3,
      "occurredAt": "2026-09-05T10:02:00.000Z",
      "entity": "account",
      "action": "update",
      "id": "{{batchAccId}}",
      "payload": { "body": { "name": "Renombrada aquí" } },
      "baseUpdatedAt": "{{batchAccVersion}}",
      "opVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "opId": "0195a000-0000-7000-8000-0000000000a2",
      "seq": 4,
      "occurredAt": "2026-09-05T10:03:00.000Z",
      "entity": "account",
      "action": "archive",
      "id": "{{batchAccId}}",
      "baseUpdatedAt": "{{batchAccVersion}}",
      "opVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "opId": "{{$guid}}",
      "seq": 5,
      "occurredAt": "2026-09-05T10:04:00.000Z",
      "entity": "category",
      "action": "create",
      "id": "{{$guid}}",
      "payload": { "body": { "name": "Batch cat {{$randomInt 100 999}}", "type": "EXPENSE" } },
      "opVersion": 1
    }
  ]
}

### Dependencia rota: la cuenta no pasa la validación (rejected VALIDATION,
### details con balance y type), el gasto que la nombra sale blocked.
POST {{baseUrl}}/sync
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "operations": [
    {
      "opId": "{{$guid}}",
      "seq": 6,
      "occurredAt": "2026-09-05T10:05:00.000Z",
      "entity": "account",
      "action": "create",
      "id": "0195a000-0000-7000-8000-0000000000b1",
      "payload": { "body": { "name": "Rota", "type": "NOPE", "balance": 10.555 } },
      "opVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "opId": "{{$guid}}",
      "seq": 7,
      "occurredAt": "2026-09-05T10:06:00.000Z",
      "entity": "transaction",
      "action": "create",
      "id": "{{$guid}}",
      "payload": { "body": { "type": "EXPENSE", "amount": 5, "date": "2026-09-01T12:00:00.000Z", "fromAccountId": "0195a000-0000-7000-8000-0000000000b1" } },
      "dependsOn": ["0195a000-0000-7000-8000-0000000000b1"],
      "opVersion": 1
    }
  ]
}

### Acción desconocida → rejected VALIDATION (field "action"); opVersion 7 → rejected
POST {{baseUrl}}/sync
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "operations": [
    { "opId": "{{$guid}}", "seq": 8, "occurredAt": "2026-09-05T10:07:00.000Z", "entity": "category", "action": "setDefault", "id": "{{$guid}}", "opVersion": 1 },
    { "opId": "{{$guid}}", "seq": 9, "occurredAt": "2026-09-05T10:07:00.000Z", "entity": "account", "action": "archive", "id": "{{$guid}}", "opVersion": 7 }
  ]
}

### ---------- Errores del sobre (400, nada se aplica) ----------

### opId repetido (400 VALIDATION)
POST {{baseUrl}}/sync
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "operations": [
    { "opId": "0195a000-0000-7000-8000-0000000000c1", "seq": 1, "occurredAt": "2026-09-05T10:00:00.000Z", "entity": "account", "action": "archive", "id": "{{$guid}}", "opVersion": 1 },
    { "opId": "0195a000-0000-7000-8000-0000000000c1", "seq": 2, "occurredAt": "2026-09-05T10:00:00.000Z", "entity": "account", "action": "archive", "id": "{{$guid}}", "opVersion": 1 }
  ]
}

### Lote vacío (400 VALIDATION)
POST {{baseUrl}}/sync
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "operations": [] }

### Sin token (401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/sync
Content-Type: application/json

{ "operations": [] }
